    <!--
      Sparkle's update feed. No <item> elements means "no updates available",
      which is the correct state until the first signed release ships.

      Each release adds one <item>, newest first:

      <item>
        <title>1.0.1</title>
        <pubDate>Tue, 05 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
        <sparkle:version>101</sparkle:version>              CFBundleVersion (build)
        <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
        <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
        <description><![CDATA[ <ul><li>What changed.</li></ul> ]]></description>
        <enclosure
          url="https://github.com/bartjan-hub/nymos-releases/releases/download/v1.0.1/Nymos-1.0.1.dmg"
          sparkle:edSignature="<from Sparkle's sign_update tool>"
          length="<exact file size in bytes>"
          type="application/octet-stream" />
      </item>

      The edSignature comes from Sparkle's `sign_update` run against the DMG
      with the private EdDSA key. That key is NOT in this repository and must
      never be committed — it lives in the Keychain on the release machine.
      Losing it means existing installs can never be updated again.
    -->
